From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:51:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] domicile: a hidden page keeps the tiles it draws

A hidden page dropped every tile (CUTOFF_ALLOW_NOTHING, a zero memory
limit). The shell hides the windows of other workspaces and other tabs
with `display: none`, so showing one again was a raster of its whole
viewport. On a laptop's GPU at battery clocks that stalled the desk's
frames in the middle of a workspace slide, 50-100 ms at a time, worst
with a heavy page and a busy machine.

- A hidden page keeps its memory limit and takes the absolute minimum
  policy (CUTOFF_ALLOW_REQUIRED_ONLY): it keeps the tiles its viewport
  draws, as a hidden native window keeps its buffer. Shown again, it
  draws from them.
- TileManager frees every other tile under that policy at once,
  whatever the limit, so a hidden page holds no prepaint.
- Its contexts still go invisible and its decodes are still freed, as
  before.
- A memory policy of zero from the GPU process still drops them all.

Covered by DomicileHiddenPageTilesTest. Guarded by
`guard-webview-reshown-tiles.sh`.

Verified: not built. This repository cannot build Chromium; the engine
job builds it on crux.

Co-Authored-By: Connor Prussin <connor@prussin.net>
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01LWjcAMeLzLP3yz4yH2gzBk
---
 cc/tiles/tile_manager.cc         | 13 +++++++++++++
 cc/trees/layer_tree_host_impl.cc | 17 +++++++++++++----
 2 files changed, 26 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/cc/tiles/tile_manager.cc b/cc/tiles/tile_manager.cc
index 6b8eed0..eaaf894 100644
--- a/cc/tiles/tile_manager.cc
+++ b/cc/tiles/tile_manager.cc
@@ -1006,6 +1006,19 @@ TileManager::PrioritizedWorkToSchedule TileManager::AssignGpuMemoryToTiles() {
       std::move(eviction_priority_queue), hard_memory_limit, &memory_usage,
       &work_to_schedule.required_for_draw_tile_state_changed);
 
+  // Domicile: the absolute minimum is the tiles drawn now, which a hidden page
+  // keeps (LayerTreeHostImpl::UpdateTileManagerMemoryPolicy). Every other tile
+  // goes at once, whatever the limit.
+  if (global_state_.memory_limit_policy == ALLOW_ABSOLUTE_MINIMUM) {
+    constexpr TilePriority kDrawnNow =
+        TilePriority(HIGH_RESOLUTION, TilePriority::NOW, 0);
+    eviction_priority_queue =
+        FreeTileResourcesWithLowerPriorityUntilUsageIsWithinLimit(
+            std::move(eviction_priority_queue), MemoryUsage(0, 0), kDrawnNow,
+            &memory_usage,
+            &work_to_schedule.required_for_draw_tile_state_changed);
+  }
+
   // At this point, if we ran out of memory when allocating resources and we
   // couldn't go past even the NOW bin, this means we have evicted resources
   // from all tiles with a lower priority while we still might have resources
diff --git a/cc/trees/layer_tree_host_impl.cc b/cc/trees/layer_tree_host_impl.cc
index 1f7f1e4..f6759ad 100644
--- a/cc/trees/layer_tree_host_impl.cc
+++ b/cc/trees/layer_tree_host_impl.cc
@@ -1979,9 +1979,16 @@ void LayerTreeHostImpl::UpdateTileManagerMemoryPolicy(
 
   global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes = 0;
   global_tile_state_.soft_memory_limit_in_bytes = 0;
-  if (visible_ && policy.bytes_limit_when_visible > 0) {
+  // Domicile: a hidden page keeps the tiles its viewport draws, as a hidden
+  // native window keeps its buffer. Windows on other workspaces and behind
+  // other tabs are hidden; shown again without them, a page rasters its whole
+  // viewport, which stalls the desk's frames on a laptop's GPU mid-slide. Its
+  // prepaint tiles still go (TileManager, patch 0252).
+  if (policy.bytes_limit_when_visible > 0) {
     global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes =
         policy.bytes_limit_when_visible;
+  }
+  if (visible_ && policy.bytes_limit_when_visible > 0) {
     global_tile_state_.soft_memory_limit_in_bytes =
         (static_cast<int64_t>(global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes) *
          settings_.max_memory_for_prepaint_percentage) /
@@ -1990,10 +1997,10 @@ void LayerTreeHostImpl::UpdateTileManagerMemoryPolicy(
   global_tile_state_.memory_limit_policy =
       ManagedMemoryPolicy::PriorityCutoffToTileMemoryLimitPolicy(
           visible_ ? policy.priority_cutoff_when_visible
-                   : gpu::MemoryAllocation::CUTOFF_ALLOW_NOTHING);
+                   : gpu::MemoryAllocation::CUTOFF_ALLOW_REQUIRED_ONLY);
   global_tile_state_.num_resources_limit = policy.num_resources_limit;
 
-  if (global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes > 0) {
+  if (visible_ && global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes > 0) {
     // If |global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes| is greater than 0, we
     // consider our contexts visible. Notify the contexts here. We handle
     // becoming invisible in NotifyAllTileTasksComplete to avoid interrupting
@@ -2285,7 +2292,9 @@ void LayerTreeHostImpl::NotifyAllTileTasksCompleted() {
 
   // The tile tasks started by the most recent call to PrepareTiles have
   // completed. Now is a good time to free resources if necessary.
-  if (global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes == 0) {
+  // Domicile: a hidden page keeps a memory limit for its tiles, so test
+  // visibility too (UpdateTileManagerMemoryPolicy).
+  if (!visible_ || global_tile_state_.hard_memory_limit_in_bytes == 0) {
     // Free image decode controller resources before notifying the
     // contexts of visibility change. This ensures that the imaged decode
     // controller has released all Skia refs at the time Skia's cleanup
